1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,789
This saber-toothed cub

2
00:00:01,789 --> 00:00:03,685
is over 35,000 years old.

3
00:00:03,895 --> 00:00:04,753
And its fur

4
00:00:04,753 --> 00:00:05,845
is still here.

5
00:00:06,055 --> 00:00:07,910
Found in Siberian permafrost,

6
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:09,754
these are preserved remains,

7
00:00:09,964 --> 00:00:11,203
not a living animal.

8
00:00:11,413 --> 00:00:12,706
Scientists studied

9
00:00:12,706 --> 00:00:14,070
its skull and teeth

10
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:15,664
using CT imaging.

11
00:00:15,874 --> 00:00:18,236
The animal was Homotherium,

12
00:00:18,446 --> 00:00:20,666
an extinct saber-toothed cat.

13
00:00:20,876 --> 00:00:22,646
Its tooth development suggests

14
00:00:22,646 --> 00:00:23,650
it was only about

15
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:24,594
three weeks old.

16
00:00:24,804 --> 00:00:25,713
Compared with a

17
00:00:25,713 --> 00:00:27,046
similar-aged lion cub,

18
00:00:27,256 --> 00:00:28,524
it had smaller ears,

19
00:00:28,734 --> 00:00:29,595
a powerful neck,

20
00:00:29,805 --> 00:00:31,233
and broader front paws.

21
00:00:31,443 --> 00:00:33,591
Those soft-tissue details are things

22
00:00:33,591 --> 00:00:35,261
a bare skeleton cannot show.

23
00:00:35,471 --> 00:00:36,968
But the mummy is incomplete.

24
00:00:37,178 --> 00:00:38,370
A full living appearance

25
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:39,712
still needs reconstruction.

26
00:00:39,922 --> 00:00:41,147
Not a resurrected predator.

27
00:00:41,357 --> 00:00:42,389
A tiny survivor

28
00:00:42,389 --> 00:00:43,284
of deep time,

29
00:00:43,494 --> 00:00:44,889
revealing what bones alone

30
00:00:44,889 --> 00:00:45,425
leave out.
